# PowerShell-safe Git commits

When creating git commits in this repo on Windows/PowerShell:

- **Command Allowlist (required on Windows):** Cursor’s sandbox blocks writes to `.git`. `required_permissions: ['all']` does **not** bypass this. For agent commits to work, add `git add` and `git commit` (or the full compound command) to **Cursor Settings → Agents → Auto-Run → Command Allowlist**, or enable **Allow Git Writes Without Approval**. Otherwise commits will always fail with "Unable to create index.lock: Permission denied".
- **Always run git as a single terminal invocation** with `required_permissions: ['all']`. Use one combined command: `git add ... ; if ($?) { git commit -m $title -m $body }`. Do **not** run `git add` and `git commit` as separate terminal commands — that doubles lock usage and contention.
- **`required_permissions: ['all']`** fixes sandbox-related "permission denied" when the **terminal** runs git. It does **not** fix lock contention when **Cursor** holds `.git/index.lock` (Source Control, background git). For that, reduce overlap:
  - **Nachhaltiger Lock-Fix:** `.vscode/settings.json` has `git.autorefresh: false` and `git.autofetch: false` → less background git. Refresh Source Control manually (Git: Refresh) when needed.
  - Prefer **terminal-only** commits (agent or user). Avoid using Source Control "Commit" or "Refresh" while the agent is committing.
- Do **not** use bash heredocs or bash-style redirections (they fail in PowerShell). Use PowerShell here-strings + `git commit -m <title> -m <body>`.

**If lock persists:** Close Cursor → delete `.git/index.lock` → reopen. If deletion fails (access denied), restart the PC so Cursor releases the handle.

## Scoped commits (common workflow)

If the user asks to "commit all changes on web" (plus main README), stage **only** `web/**` and `README.md`.

- Do **not** stage/commit `.cursor/**` unless explicitly requested.
- Do **not** stage/commit untracked `scripts/` unless explicitly requested.

## Example (run as ONE terminal command with `required_permissions: ['all']`)

```powershell
$title = '[TAG] component: short description'
$body = @'
WHY: Explain why this change was made.

Optional details if needed.
'@
git add -- "README.md" "web"; if ($?) { git commit -m $title -m $body }
```
